<title>SWITZERLAND: Tietmeyer sees progress against counterfeiting.</title>
<headline>Tietmeyer sees progress against counterfeiting.</headline>
<dateline>BASLE, Switzerland 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Bundesbank President Hans Tietmeyer said on Monday he expected further progress in technologies to protect against counterfeiting of bank notes.</p>
<p>Speaking to reporters in his capacity as chairman of the Group of 10 (G-10 ) central bank governors committee, Tietmeyer said the governors had heard a report on modern reproduction technologies for banknotes and how these can protect against counterfeiting.</p>
<p>&quot;It is useful to see what can be done and I think there will be more protection against counterfeiting. I hope so,&quot; Tietmeyer said.</p>
<p>-- Frankfurt Newsroom + 49 69 756525</p>
</text>
